Title: Defer pcap flushing from SIGUSR2 handler
Body:
## Summary

`SIGUSR2` currently calls `pcap_dump_flush()` from a signal handler. If the signal arrives while `pcap_dump()` is writing a packet, the two operations can corrupt the dump.

Defer the flush to the capture loop: the handler requests a break, the loop flushes outside the handler, then resumes capture. The callback protects packet writes from `SIGUSR2`, and tracks packets handled across interrupted `pcap_loop()` calls so `-c` still stops at the requested count.

Add a regression test that sends repeated `SIGUSR2` signals during a slow dump and checks the resulting packet contents and count.

Fixes #1231.

## Testing

- `make -s`
- `make -s check` — 793 passed, 13 skipped
- `git diff --check`

Files (3): tcpdump.c, tests/TESTflushpcap, tests/TESTrun
